<title>USA: Integral Systems stock split approved.</title>
<headline>Integral Systems stock split approved.</headline>
<dateline>LANHAM, Md. 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Integral Systems Inc said Thursday that its shareholders approved a three-for-one stock split and an increase in authorized common shares to 10 million from two million at the company's annual meeting.</p>
<p>The split, to be completed by July 1, will increase the number of authorized shares to 10 million from two million, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Based in Lanham, the company provides satellite ground systems.</p>
</text>
